.TITLE "df"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Reports the amount of disk space used and available on filesystems. It provides a high-level overview of __storage consumption__ across all mounted drives.

.DIV "TLDR"
**df**
Displays the disk usage for all currently mounted filesystems.
> 

**df -h**
Displays disk usage in human-readable formats like GB or MB.
> __-h__ human-readable flag

**df -T**
Includes the filesystem type (e.g., ext4, xfs) in the output.
> __-T__ type flag

**df path**
Displays the disk usage for the filesystem containing a specific path.
> __path__ a file or directory location

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __df -h__ is the most common way to quickly check if a disk is becoming full. It is important to remember that __df__ shows filesystem-level usage, which may differ slightly from individual directory measurements.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:du** **linux:lsblk** **linux:mount**

